<transactionbodycustomfield scriptid="custbody_arch_ready_to_build">
  <!--
    CWP ARCH "Ready to Build". The trader ticks this on a Sales Order to say the
    order is ready for the warehouse to pull and build. MANUAL, never computed —
    Marc-Antoine, 2026-09-10 call at [30:26]: "c'est manuel, c'est le trader qui
    dit genre c'est ready to build."

    ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, added 2026-09-14 ──────────────────────────────────
    The field was created BY HAND in sandbox on 2026-09-11 from a throwaway SDF
    project, and until today nothing in this repo could recreate it. Two
    consequences, both real:
      1. A sandbox refresh deletes it and nothing here can put it back. What
         fires when it vanishes is the refusal at archOrderCreate.js:1390, which
         tells the trader the field "has not been created in NetSuite" — true,
         but it reads like a permanent state rather than a lost object.
      2. It could never reach PRODUCTION, where it still does not exist.
         Go-live is 1 October.

    ⚠️ DO NOT reuse custbody_so_ready_to_ship (12056) instead. That is
    Marc-Antoine's own field, a LATER stage of the flow, already written by
    MR 5544 on a schedule with no subsidiary or segment guard, so a trader's
    tick would be overwritten by the batch. Rejected to the client in writing
    on 2026-08-13.

    ── PROVENANCE OF THE VALUES BELOW ──────────────────────────────────────────
    Read off the LIVE sandbox field, internal id 14083, via a SOAP get on
    CustomizationRef (same TBA passport nsfile.mjs uses; needs no SuiteCloud
    authid). Confirmed from that read: accesslevel 2, searchlevel 2, displaytype
    NORMAL, fieldtype CHECKBOX, storevalue T, showinlist F, globalsearch F,
    isparent F, ismandatory F, checkspelling F, defaultchecked F, isformula F,
    subtab Main, bodysale T with every other bodyX false, and the label and help
    verbatim.

    The ELEMENT SET and its alphabetical order come from this account's own
    object:import dialect, copied from
      Tasks/Task 3 - Profitability Report/src/Objects/transactionbodycustomfields/
      custbody_mcgi_cm_source_so.xml
    which was produced by a real import on 2026-07-27. The eight custcol_*.xml
    files in this folder use a trimmed hand-written shape; do NOT copy those,
    SDF fills omitted elements with its own defaults on deploy.

    ⚠️ STILL INFERRED, and a deploy WILL write them: applyformatting F,
    encryptatrest F, empty description, and the element set itself (which bodyX
    elements exist, the presence of aidescription / enabletextenhance /
    fldsizelabel, the absence of bodyexpensereport / bodystore). All of that came
    from an import of a DIFFERENT field. Settle it with a read-only import of
    THIS one as soon as the SuiteCloud authid is restored: run suitecloud
    object:import for type transactionbodycustomfield, scriptid
    custbody_arch_ready_to_build, into a scratch destinationfolder, then diff
    against this file before any deploy that includes it. (The flags are spelled
    out in prose rather than shown, because a double hyphen cannot appear inside
    an XML comment and putting the real command here makes this file unparseable.)

    ── TWO THINGS THAT ARE NOT COSMETIC ────────────────────────────────────────
    searchlevel 2: the warehouse split queue reads this field under the
    warehouse user's OWN role (customscript_mcgi_sl_warehouse_react has an empty
    runasrole and allemployees=T), and archSplitQueue.readyToBuildBySo FAILS
    CLOSED. A role that cannot search this field therefore sees an empty queue,
    not an error.

    displaytype NORMAL: SDF refuses both INLINE and DISABLED for this object
    type and fails the whole deploy. Proven against prod on 2026-07-27 with the
    field named above, and not caused by accesslevel.

    ── OPEN UX GAP, and SDF CANNOT CLOSE IT ────────────────────────────────────
    Measured on a live Sales Order 2026-09-14: on the VIEW page,
    custbody_so_ready_to_ship (12056, Marc-Antoine's own field) renders as a live
    INPUT, so a user ticks it inline without opening the record. THIS field
    renders "inputreadonly" inside a span, so it needs Edit, tick, Save.

    That is a worse interaction than the field he already uses for the identical
    gesture, and he asked on the 2026-09-10 call at [30:26] where he ticks this
    one. Closing it means an MGSL administrator changing the Display Type in the
    NetSuite UI (Customization > Lists, Records, and Fields > Transaction Body
    Fields).

    ⚠️ AND IT WILL BE REVERTED BY THE NEXT DEPLOY OF THIS OBJECT, because
    displaytype must stay NORMAL here for SDF to accept the file at all. Exactly
    the trap custbody_mcgi_cm_source_so documents: prod is deliberately not
    NORMAL, set by hand, and redeploying reverts it. If the Display Type is ever
    changed by hand, re-apply it after any deploy that includes this object, or
    leave the object out of deploy.xml once it is live.

    ── FORM MEMBERSHIP IS NOT EXPRESSED HERE ───────────────────────────────────
    Whether a given role sees this on a given Sales Order form is a FORM
    property, not a field property, and there is no form XML in this repo.
    Measured 2026-09-14: systemnote holds six writes to this field, four of them
    context UIF (the NetSuite UI form) under role 3, so it is already reachable
    on a form for an Administrator. Whether the ARCH trader role sees it is
    UNVERIFIED — reading form membership needs object:import, which needs the
    authid.
  -->
